KNOWNBUG gnu-extensions libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ run time: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
could not be evaluated
static assertion failed
^warning: ignoring
--
GCC evaluates __builtin_memcmp in a constant expression, as libstdc++ 11's
char_traits<char>::compare does in a constexpr function.  The constant
evaluator now evaluates it over constant arrays (string literals, constexpr
arrays), comparing bytes as unsigned char.
